From 9a24cc871dccb1869714b1e26bdbb968b055caef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <2.03348624e+08+yaegerbomb42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:55:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vm): resolve workspace symlinks in the container and keep
 the VNC password out of PID 1 (VM-10)

The /workspace confinement was lexical: resolveWorkspacePath() rejected ".."
but the driver then ran cat/stat/head on the raw path, so a workspace symlink
to /proc/1/environ (SWARM_VNC_PASSWORD) or /etc/passwd was followed and served
through the files, report-artifact and lenses routes.

- docker-driver: every file op resolves the path inside the container with
  realpath -e (readlink -f fallback) and refuses anything outside /workspace
  with VmPathError("outside_workspace"); reads open the resolved path, writes
  resolve the parent and refuse a symlink at the destination (test -L).
- files/artifacts routes answer 403 for a refused path; the lenses route drops
  a refused artifact from the model context.
- Desktop VNC password: containers are now created with `docker create`, the
  password is copied in as a 0600 node-owned file, then `docker start` runs
  init.sh, which reads and deletes it. The password is no longer passed in the
  container environment (/proc/1/environ), and the image/docs are updated.
- FakeVmDriver models symlinks (link()/seedFile()) so route tests can assert
  refusals; driver and route tests cover escape and in-workspace cases.

Refs b13 (VM-10)
